                <pb facs="0215" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4 A 2/110: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary General of the League of Nations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Drummond</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1924-10-15T12:36:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1924-09-17T14:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>].<lb/>[Received October 15, 1924—12:36
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Reference my letter C. L. 5, 14th January, 1924. Would remind you no reply yet
                    received. Answer would facilitate preliminary arrangements conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Drummond</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
